          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em closure operator
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            on a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset+of+subobjects"} poset of subobjects
            (of some
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logic"} logic
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+operator"} modal operator
            %em closed
            (or perhaps
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modal+type"} modal
          %p
            Dually, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            on a poset is called a
            %em co-closure operator
            and the elements fixed by it are called
            = succeed "." do
              %em co-closed
          %p
            More generally, in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent monad
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            as being a closure operator, and of any idempotent
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonad"} comonad
            as a co-closure operator.
          %h2#definition Definition
          #ClosureOperatorAsMonad.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              %strong closure operator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋄
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \diamond
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/idempotent+monad"} idempotent monad
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋄
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \diamond \colon \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{C}
              equipped with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+a+monad"} unit
              and product
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformations"} natural transformations
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mo ⋄
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi id
                          %mi 𝒞
                        %mo →
                        %mo ⋄
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_{\diamond} \;\colon\; id_{\mathcal{C}} \to \diamond
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi μ
                          %mo ⋄
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⋄
                        %mo ∘
                        %mo ⋄
                        %mo →
                        %mo ⋄
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{\diamond} \;\colon\; \diamond \circ \diamond \to \diamond
            %p
              such that the
              = succeed "-axioms" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the product map is an
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi η
                          %mrow
                            %mo ⋄
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_{\diamond(-)}
                  is an isomorphism.
          #ClosureAndClosedObjects.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⋄
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \diamond \colon \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{C}
              a closure operator, def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClosureOperatorAsMonad"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in \mathcal{C}
              an object, we say that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ⋄
                        %mi X
                        %mo ∈
