                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msup
                        %mi E
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(-, \Omega) \colon E^{op} \to Set
                provides an example of a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+closure+operator"} universal closure operator
          %h2#InducedClosureOnSlices Induced closure on slices
          %p
            We discuss here how a closure operator on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
            may induce closure operators on each of its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+categories"} slice categories
          %p
